| Priority | Issue                                                                | Type          | Impact                                     |
| -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| **P0**   | Scoped package missing `publishConfig.access` / `--access public`    | Config / CI   | Release will fail on npm (HTTP 402)        |
| **P0**   | `tsup` generates `any` types, dropping `src/types/index.d.ts`        | Types / Build | TypeScript consumers get zero intellisense |
| **P0**   | Uncaught `TypeError` on `null` rules or non-string date keys         | Stability     | Application crash in common usage          |
| **P1**   | `parseTime` accepts > 24:00 times, causing 24/7 hijack               | Logic / Bug   | Erroneous rule permanently takes over      |
| **P1**   | Single date+time composite rule wraps around all day                 | Logic / Bug   | Halloween 6 PM rule activates at 8 AM      |
| **P1**   | Missing `"use client";` in React entry point                         | Framework     | Incompatible with Next.js App Router       |
| **P1**   | SSR hydration mismatch & README vs code contradiction                | Architecture  | Next.js hydration warning / layout flash   |
| **P2**   | `JSON.stringify` on every render in `useAutoTheme`                   | Performance   | Main thread lag on large rule sets         |
| **P2**   | Rule resolution logic duplicated in `css-vars.js`                    | Architecture  | Logic drift and dual maintenance           |
| **P2**   | `examples/html-css-vars` duplicate `setInterval`                     | Bug / Example | Memory and timer leaks in demo             |
| **P2**   | Rule matching without `style` returns `undefined`                    | Edge Case     | Breaks fallback behavior                   |
| **P3**   | Missing standard `package.json` fields (`repository`, `sideEffects`) | Standards     | Warnings on install, poor SEO/npm metrics  |
| **P3**   | Missing CI testing workflow on pull requests                         | DevOps        | Untested code can merge unnoticed          |
| **P3**   | `README.md` badge reads `LICENSE-CUSTOM`                             | Docs          | Confusion about licensing                  |
| **P3**   | `stop()` does not reset DOM classes/vars                             | Polish / SPA  | Leftover styles on route changes           |

Ready to systematically implement and resolve these items whenever you're ready to proceed.
